    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="0971" n="867" xml:id="pg867"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.6461 Tsana Dam/268: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ethiopia (Southard) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1931-05-06T16:00:00+02:35">May 6, 1931—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 7—8:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9. Referring to my cable of April 27, 4 p.m., British Chargé d’Affaires has had a
                    reply from London informing him that the Sudan Government considers it premature
                    to press at this time for a conference. Chargé d’Affaires does not intend to say
                    anything to the Ethiopians unless further instructed. In connection with this
                    delay please see my despatch No. 657 of March 7th<anchor n="16" xml:id="d646-f1"
                    /> and related despatches.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Southard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
